CEO John Ternus is making changes to Apple's leadership, reports <em><a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-08/apple-names-steve-smith-m-a-chief-moves-adrian-perica-to-services-business">Bloomberg</a></em>. Apple veteran Steve Smith will take over mergers and acquisitions and corporate development, which was previously led by Adrian Perica. M&A is an important team at Apple, handling acquisitions and arrangements like the deal Apple had with OpenAI to add ChatGPT to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/John-Ternus-and-Rainbow-Countour-Apple-Logo.jpg" alt="" width="1324" height="744" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062102" /><br/>
Perica will stay at Apple to oversee <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/icloud/">iCloud</a>, Fitness+, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-news/">Apple News</a>, which he has done since 2023, and will now report to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/app-store/">App Store</a> and services lead <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/eddy-cue/">Eddy Cue</a>. While Perica reported to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/tim-cook/">Tim Cook</a> in his M&A role, Smith will report to Apple CFO Kevan Parekh as M&A moves back to the finance division.<br/>
<br/>
Carson Oliver is being promoted to vice president of the &zwnj;App Store&zwnj;, and he has been in charge of the &zwnj;App Store&zwnj; since <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/phil-schiller/">Phil Schiller</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/31/phil-schiller-stepping-down-app-store/">stepped down from his role</a> as &zwnj;App Store&zwnj; chief in late August. Oliver is reporting to Cue, who is now overseeing the &zwnj;App Store&zwnj; and other services.<br/>
<br/>
